<title>JAPAN: M'bishi launches Dutch-made car in Japan.</title>
<headline>M'bishi launches Dutch-made car in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Motors Corp said it launched its Dutch-made Carisma four-door compact sedan in Japan on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Carisma, with a 1.8-litre engine, is made by Dutch joint venture NedCar, which equally owned by Mitsubishi, AB Volvo, and the Dutch government.</p>
<p>It is the third European-made Japanese brand to go on sale in Japan. Nissan Motor Co Ltd already sells the British-made Primera and the Spanish-made Mistral.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi said it hopes to sell 1,000 of the Carismas a month at prices starting at 1.548 million yen.</p>
</text>
